Pokemon scarlet and violet is just  around the corner and with it are some  sweeping changes coming to the Pokemon  formula here are 11 of the biggest  changes we've found so far number one a  seamless open world Pokemon scarlet and  violet is shaping up to be the first  truly open world Pokemon game Arceus  which was released earlier this year has  a handful of open areas but they were  separated by loading screens and this  adventure players will be able to  explore a seamless world at their own  Leisure as a longtime Pokemon fan this  is exciting news Arceus kind of  scratched this itch back in January but  scarlet and Violet's open world seems to  be a lot more ambitious although some of  those textures look a little whack  number two non-linear progression there  are three major stories you can chase in  scarlet and violet Victory Road Starfall  Street and path of Legends Victory Road  is the good old gym challenge that has  you defeat eight gym leaders however  unlike every other Mainline game in the  series it seems as though you can tackle  gyms in any order you see fit though if  this is the case we still aren't sure  how the gym challenge will be balanced  will the gym leaders team change  depending on how many badges you have or  will some gyms be way too hard from the  outset if a gym Leader's Pokemon scales  and level does that also mean they could  have different teams depending on when  you challenge them one thing we do know  is that due to terrestrializing a new  feature I'll talk about in a little bit  a gym leader could feasibly use any  Pokemon regardless of its initial type  as long as it has the correct Terror  type in a couple trailers we saw  brassius the grass type gym leader use  the rock type Pokemon sudowuru now we'll  touch on the other major story lines  later in the video so stay  number three Champion rank once you've  defeated all eight gym leaders you can  take a champion assessment we aren't  entirely sure what this assessment  entails but I imagine it will be similar  to the Elite Four in previous games if  you complete it you'll achieve Champion  Rank and you'll be able to challenge  other Champion ranked trainers  throughout the region hopefully this  means that we'll get some challenging  post-game battles outside of the tried  and true battle tower number 4 to  rasterize Pokemon that brings us to  terasterizing this allows you to change  a Pokemon's type mid battle using  something called a Terra orb you can  only use this orb once per battle and it  must be recharged after use every  Pokemon in the paudia region has a  terror type and a Pokemon's Terror type  can be any of the 18 different types  meaning every Pokemon can rasterize and  potentially change its type mid battle  the best way to get Pokemon with rare  Terra types is either by finding  sparkling Pokemon in the wild like this  Jigglypuff or by doing Terror raid  battles which are multiplayer battles  that allow you to catch powerful Pokemon  on with rare Terra types generally it  seems like common Pokemon you find in  the wild will have a terror type that  matches one of their original types  while rare Pokemon have a Terra type  that's different I'm really curious to  see how this affects the meta especially  at higher level play hopefully we'll see  some really creative teams at the  professional level number five Titan  Pokemon along with the Victory Road  questline you'll be helping a new  character named Arvin gather a rare  ingredient called Urban mystica in the  path of Legends quest the catch is not  that these herbs will get you high but  that they are guarded by Titan Pokemon  these Titan Pokemon are much bigger than  normal and offer a greater challenge  based on the trailer and the position of  the Pokemon's HP bar it looks like these  will be treated as boss battles  scattered throughout the world it also  looks like you'll need to find and  challenge some of these Pokemon multiple  times as cloth in the trailer scurries  away when his health gets low number six  Starfall Street the third quest line  revolves around team star a group of  class cutting delinquents as the  official Pokemon website puts it who  have formed a series of bases around the  paldeo region as most young Pokemon  trainers do when they are confronted by  a dangerous group of shady individuals  you'll need to challenge them to Pokemon  battles however these battles could play  out a little differently in the most  recent trailer we saw a trainer enter a  Starfall base and kick off a large-scale  Auto Battle it looks like in these  situations you'll be able to send out  two Pokemon at a time to battle for you  though battles do return to normal once  you confront the base's boss number 7  auto battles you heard me right Auto  Battles Pokemon scarlet and violet  introduces the let's go feature this  allows you to send out your lead Pokemon  to gather items and take on wild Pokemon  on its own to earn XP it's important to  note that this is different from sword  and Shield's polka jobs that allowed you  to send out Pokemon on their own through  a PC let's go happens in real time  meaning you can follow your partner  Pokemon if you'd like or you can take  care of other Pokemon related business  personally I'll probably avoid doing  this because if one of my Pokemon  automatically knocks out a shiny I will  be livid number eight crafting crafting  was already an Arceus but scarlet and  violet will allow you to craft TMS with  items you collect from battling and  catching Pokemon at every Pokemon Center  you'll find a green PC that will allow  you to either craft TMS or exchange  materials for League points it appears  every TM will require resources from a  specific Pokemon and something called  League points both can be earned and  collected through catching and battling  Pokemon number nine picnics Pokemon  scarlet and violet will let you host a  picnic with your beloved Pokemon in many  ways these picnics feel like expanded  versions of camps from sword and shield  you can bathe them play with them and  feed them during a picnic you can make a  sandwich with some of the ingredients  you've gathered during your adventure  look there's even ham sandwiches will  give your Pokemon party passive XP Buffs  as well as make certain types easier to  catch Additionally you can sometimes  find eggs in your picnic basket it's  unclear if this happens by random or if  egg breeding now takes place during a  picnic seems a little unhygienic to me  but hey if that means I don't have to  keep a running back to Pokemon breeders  that's A-Okay by me number 10  multiplayer multiplayer has been a  staple of the Pokemon series since red  and blue scarlet and violet is taking it  to the next level with Co-op play  players will be able to explore the  world with up to three friends now we  aren't sure how standard turn-based  battles will work while your friends are  mosing about the world but it should be  interesting nonetheless along with  trading and battling you can also take  on terror raid battles with fellow  trainers like the raids in Pokemon sword  and shield these let you team up with  some friends in order to defeat and  catch a rare Pokemon unlike sword and  shield though these battles seem to play  out a little differently than regular  turn-based battles number 11 changes to  legendaries the legendary Pokemon always  play a huge role in these games however  it looks like you might be teaming up  with the mascot legendaries Corydon and  Mariah ride on at the very beginning of  your adventure it's hard to say when  you'll first encounter these Pokemon but  considering how important they are for  traversal I think it's safe to say that  you'll meet both of them within the  first couple hours both legendaries take  the form of motorcycles although Corydon  despite having Wheels uses his legs to  move I was torn on which version to get  until I saw this I will be getting  Violet thank you very much and there it  is 11 of the biggest changes coming to  Pokemon scarlet and violet let us know  what you're most excited about in the  comments below personally I can't wait  to see how this non-linear story  progression shakes out scarlet and  violet hits shelves on November 18th  this year so stay tuned to Gamespot  because we have plenty more Pokemon  coverage coming your way very soon  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  [Music]
 

